theory_blocks.body:
This mass-proportion method answers 'if this much reacts, how much of that is needed or made', using only a balanced equation and Mr values; [[blue:it never needs to mention how many particles are actually present]].

The next lesson introduces a counting unit, the **mole**, which connects a measured mass directly to a number of particles. The reacting-mass method used here still works once moles are introduced;

moles simply explain, underneath, why the proportions work in the first place.

